# 🛠️ Help Desk Command Cheat Sheet

> **Windows Command Prompt & PowerShell Reference**  
> A quick-reference guide for common networking, system administration, troubleshooting, and Active Directory commands.

---

## 🌐 Command Prompt — Networking

| 💻 Command | 📋 Purpose |
|---|---|
| `ipconfig` | Displays the computer's IP address and basic network configuration |
| `ipconfig /all` | Displays detailed network information, including MAC address, DNS, and DHCP |
| `ipconfig /release` | Releases the current DHCP-assigned IP address |
| `ipconfig /renew` | Requests a new IP address from the DHCP server |
| `ipconfig /flushdns` | Clears the local DNS resolver cache |
| `ping 8.8.8.8` | Tests basic network connectivity to an IP address |
| `tracert google.com` | Displays the network hops between your computer and a destination |
| `nslookup google.com` | Tests DNS resolution and displays DNS information |
| `netstat -an` | Displays active connections and listening ports |

### 🔎 Common Networking Workflow

```text
No Internet?
    │
    ├── ipconfig
    │      ↓
    ├── ping 127.0.0.1
    │      ↓
    ├── ping <default-gateway>
    │      ↓
    ├── ping 8.8.8.8
    │      ↓
    └── nslookup google.com
```

---

## 🖥️ Command Prompt — System & Files

| 💻 Command | 📋 Purpose |
|---|---|
| `hostname` | Displays the computer's hostname |
| `whoami` | Displays the currently logged-in user |
| `systeminfo` | Displays detailed OS, hardware, and system information |
| `tasklist` | Lists currently running processes |
| `taskkill /IM notepad.exe /F` | Forcefully terminates a running process |
| `sfc /scannow` | Scans and repairs protected Windows system files |
| `chkdsk` | Checks the file system and disk for errors |
| `gpupdate /force` | Forces Group Policy to refresh |
| `gpresult /r` | Displays the Group Policy settings applied to the computer/user |
| `net user username` | Displays information about a local user account |

---

# ⚡ PowerShell

## 🖥️ Processes & Services

| 💻 Command | 📋 Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Get-Process` | Lists currently running processes |
| `Get-Service` | Lists Windows services and their status |
| `Restart-Service -Name Spooler` | Restarts the Print Spooler service |
| `Get-Help Get-Service` | Displays help and usage information for a PowerShell command |

---

## 🌐 PowerShell Networking

| 💻 Command | 📋 Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Test-NetConnection google.com` | Tests network connectivity to a destination |
| `Test-NetConnection google.com -Port 443` | Tests connectivity to a specific TCP port |
| `Resolve-DnsName google.com` | Performs DNS resolution |
| `Get-NetIPConfiguration` | Displays IP configuration information |
| `Get-NetAdapter` | Displays network adapters and their status |

---

## 👤 Active Directory

> **Requires the Active Directory PowerShell module.**

| 💻 Command | 📋 Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Get-ADUser -Identity username` | Retrieves information about an Active Directory user |
| `Get-ADUser -Identity username -Properties LockedOut` | Checks whether an AD account is locked |
| `Unlock-ADAccount -Identity username` | Unlocks a locked Active Directory account |
| `Set-ADAccountPassword -Identity username -Reset -NewPassword (Read-Host -AsSecureString)` | Resets an AD user's password |
| `Get-ADGroupMember -Identity "GroupName"` | Lists the members of an Active Directory group |
| `Get-ADComputer -Identity "ComputerName"` | Retrieves information about an AD computer account |

---

# 🚨 Quick Troubleshooting Reference

### 🌐 Network Problem

```powershell
ipconfig /all
ping <default-gateway>
ping 8.8.8.8
nslookup google.com
```

### 👤 User Account Problem

```powershell
whoami
net user username
```

For Active Directory:

```powershell
Get-ADUser -Identity username -Properties LockedOut
Unlock-ADAccount -Identity username
```

### 🖨️ Printer Problem

```powershell
Get-Service -Name Spooler
Restart-Service -Name Spooler
```

### 🏢 Group Policy Problem

```cmd
gpupdate /force
gpresult /r
```

---

## 📌 Command Categories

| Category | Primary Tools |
|---|---|
| 🌐 Networking | `ipconfig`, `ping`, `tracert`, `nslookup` |
| 🖥️ System | `systeminfo`, `tasklist`, `sfc`, `chkdsk` |
| ⚙️ Services | `Get-Service`, `Restart-Service` |
| 👤 Users | `whoami`, `net user`, `Get-ADUser` |
| 🔐 Active Directory | `Get-ADUser`, `Unlock-ADAccount`, `Get-ADGroupMember` |
| 🏢 Group Policy | `gpupdate`, `gpresult` |
| 🖨️ Printing | `Restart-Service Spooler` |
| 🌐 PowerShell Networking | `Test-NetConnection`, `Resolve-DnsName`, `Get-NetAdapter` |

---

> **💡 Tip:** When troubleshooting, start with the simplest command that can confirm or eliminate a possible cause. Document what you checked and what the result was.
